#title["Sometimes it's better not to tell the truth"]

It is almost certain that everyone has at some point stood before this question. Whether to tell a difficult truth, or to omit it and tell a lie instead. Is there a definite answer though?

Some people, who try to minimize harm and are fine with lying with a good cause in mind, say it is acceptable. They believe it is the lesser evil and that it is in fact very rational to omit the truth. I believe most people think this way.

On the other side, there are others, who value truth and honesty over everything else. They believe that while difficult to take in at first, in the longterm, telling the truth is more beneficial to everyone involved. While they may come off as rude in the beginning, people can begin to value their firm stance over time.

I personally can't identify with either of those two extremes, but I tend to aspire to that of the second group. I believe that it is very easy fall into the trap of empathy that can cause you to normalize lying in everyday life in a way. I am convinced that overcoming these tendencies is a crucial part in maturing as an individual.
